    "uploaded": []
  },
  "modificationGoal": "Check fidelity, readable labels, layout and connections against the original request.",
  "advisoryPlan": "### Advisory Plan\n\n**1. Nodes & Elements**\n*   **Initial State Marker:** Unnamed solid dot (compiler-owned shape: small filled circle).\n*   **State Nodes (Rounded Rectangles):**\n    *   `Idle`\n    *   `Running`\n    *   `Paused`\n    *   `Completed`\n*   **Note:** All nodes use the compiler-defined rounded rectangle shape with fill `#e5efeb` and stroke `#355c53`. No distinct \"terminal\" styling is applied to `Completed` as it has an outgoing transition.\n\n**2. Relationships (Transitions)**\nAll connections are orthogonal polylines with filled triangle arrows (`#355c53`). Labels are event names, not actions.\n\n*   **Initial → Idle:** Entry arrow from unnamed dot to `Idle`.\n*   **Idle → Running:** Label `start`.\n*   **Running → Paused:** Label `pause`.\n*   **Paused → Running:** Label `resume`.\n*   **Running → Completed:** Label `finish`.\n*   **Paused → Idle:** Label `cancel`.\n*   **Completed → Idle:** Label `reset`.\n\n**3. Layout Strategy**\n*   **Direction:** RIGHT (Adaptable hint).\n*   **Topology:** The graph contains a primary forward path (`Idle`→`Running`→`Completed`) with a side loop (`Running`↔`Paused`) and two return paths to `Idle` (`Paused`→`Idle`, `Completed`→`Idle`).\n*   **Arrangement:** To minimize edge crossings and maintain readability of the \"teaching example\":\n    *   `Idle` is positioned leftmost (entry point).\n    *   `Running` is central.\n    *   `Paused` is placed vertically adjacent to `Running` (e.g., below) to handle the `pause`/`resume` cycle cleanly without crossing the main flow.\n    *   `Completed` is placed to the right of `Running`.\n    *   Return edges (`cancel`, `reset`) will route around the periphery (top or bottom) to avoid intersecting the central `Running`↔`Paused` or `Idle`→`Running` edges.\n\n**4. Compliance & Constraints Check**\n*   **Renderer Contract:** Uses fixed palette (`#e5efeb` fill, `#355c53` stroke/text), Noto Sans font, orthogonal arrows. No shadows/filters.\n*   **Methodology:** Preserves all 4 states and 6 transitions exactly. `Completed` is treated as a standard state node (not terminal). English text only.\n*   **Reference Usage:** Structural design only (state transition topology). No data/colors/fonts transferred from the Boolean network reference.\n*   **Avoidance:** No invented numbers or scientific conclusions.\n\n**5. Uncertainties / Renderer Limitations**\n*   **Edge Routing:** The `Completed`→`Idle` (reset) and `Paused`→`Idle` (cancel) edges create a cycle back to the start. In a strict orthogonal layout, these long backward edges may require significant routing space to avoid overlapping the `Idle`→`Running` edge. The ELK layout engine will determine the specific routing; if overlap occurs, it is a topological constraint of the provided data, not a planning error.\n*   **Node Sizing:** Text length varies (`Completed` vs `Idle`). Node widths will differ based on label content; vertical alignment of centers is not guaranteed but horizontal flow is prioritized.",
